#![forbid(unsafe_code)]

//! One token, generated by this bundle and returned over the real transport.
//!
//! Everything below the request is production code driving this package. The
//! deployment is read by the same function the serving command calls, so the
//! frontend, the tokenizer, and the model policy all come out of the package the
//! verifier accepted. The generation worker builds the real engine over this
//! bundle's own exported V1 API table, wrapped in the host's own model-executor
//! adapter, sized from the KV geometry and the vocabulary this package declares.
//! The transport is `runtime_server::serve` on a loopback port.
//!
//! What the fixture supplies is the row: a bounded synthetic row of TP4's
//! declared width whose peak is a non-special filler token. So the assertion at
//! the end is exact. The completion carries the text that filler decodes to,
//! which is the token this bundle's own operation put at the top of a
//! 154,880-wide row that the shared sampler then sampled.
//!
//! The device work happens in host memory. This proves the serving path, not a
//! GPU: package verification and the module-loading path are separate gates.

